    {
      "id": "section:0/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Kernel Core Internals",
      "source_hash": 15846181736380943852,
      "context_hash": 16336300389789279476,
      "translation": "커널 코어 내부 구조",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086508Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The glue that holds every subsystem together: boot, logging, parameters, panics, and module init",
      "source_hash": 17696027167632927288,
      "context_hash": 14673744333851561271,
      "translation": "모든 서브시스템을 하나로 묶는 접착제: 부팅, 로깅, 파라미터, 패닉, 모듈 초기화",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "panic": "패닉",
        "subsystem": "서브시스템"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086508Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "What is \"kernel core\"?",
      "source_hash": 14357736886402235218,
      "context_hash": 6588661128247027424,
      "translation": "\"커널 코어\"란 무엇입니까?",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086508Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The kernel core is the collection of infrastructure that does not belong to any single subsystem but that every subsystem depends on.",
      "source_hash": 7573499708999963460,
      "context_hash": 17474509435411268930,
      "translation": "커널 코어는 특정 서브시스템 하나에 속하지 않지만 모든 서브시스템이 의존하는 인프라의 집합입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널",
        "subsystem": "서브시스템"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086509Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "It lives primarily in `init/`, `kernel/`, and `arch/x86/kernel/` (and the equivalent arch directories), and it answers the question: *how does a compressed binary become a running operating system that can schedule tasks, respond to interrupts, and load drivers?*",
      "source_hash": 7427157598683889012,
      "context_hash": 14193029427314604986,
      "translation": "주로 `init/`, `kernel/`, `arch/x86/kernel/`(및 이에 해당하는 다른 arch 디렉터리)에 있으며, 다음 질문에 답합니다: *압축된 바이너리가 어떻게 태스크를 스케줄링하고, 인터럽트에 응답하고, 드라이버를 로드할 수 있는 실행 중인 운영체제가 됩니까?*",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "interrupt": "인터럽트"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086509Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "Topics covered here include:",
      "source_hash": 2754961622403086355,
      "context_hash": 11912351451184021192,
      "translation": "여기에서 다루는 주제는 다음과 같습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "The C entry point (`start_kernel()`) and the ordered sequence of subsystem initialization calls it drives",
      "source_hash": 15313682917152368210,
      "context_hash": 16666612554063070701,
      "translation": "C 진입점(`start_kernel()`)과 이 함수가 이끄는 서브시스템 초기화 호출의 순서",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "entry point": "진입점",
        "subsystem": "서브시스템"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "How the kernel receives and parses boot parameters from the bootloader",
      "source_hash": 1784987671924306163,
      "context_hash": 14702144361506632980,
      "translation": "커널이 부트로더로부터 부트 파라미터를 받아 파싱하는 방법",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "boot parameter": "부트 파라미터"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "How modules and built-in subsystems register their initialization functions through the initcall mechanism",
      "source_hash": 5356225514008332329,
      "context_hash": 13927420155690981718,
      "translation": "모듈과 빌트인 서브시스템이 initcall 메커니즘을 통해 초기화 함수를 등록하는 방법",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "initcall": "initcall",
        "subsystem": "서브시스템"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:6/seg:0",
      "source": "What happens when something goes catastrophically wrong — oops, panic, and crash dump collection",
      "source_hash": 2035426950981339627,
      "context_hash": 5324016706977254485,
      "translation": "심각한 오류가 발생했을 때 일어나는 일 — oops, 패닉, 크래시 덤프 수집",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "oops": "oops",
        "panic": "패닉"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T23:30:44.010670Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:7/seg:0",
      "source": "The `printk` logging infrastructure that underpins every diagnostic message in the kernel",
      "source_hash": 1816151698192757333,
      "context_hash": 13652248474601616721,
      "translation": "커널의 모든 진단 메시지를 뒷받침하는 `printk` 로깅 인프라",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:8/seg:0",
      "source": "This is not memory management, not the scheduler, not networking — it is the machinery that sets up all of those before handing control off to them.",
      "source_hash": 6173766197790556909,
      "context_hash": 1623029789479864396,
      "translation": "이것은 메모리 관리도, 스케줄러도, 네트워킹도 아닙니다 — 이 모든 것을 설정한 뒤 제어권을 넘겨주는 기반 장치입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "memory management": "메모리 관리",
        "scheduler": "스케줄러"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:15:06.086510Z",
      "issues": []
    },
